      ":question/problem": "If $Q$ is a $5\\times 7$ matrix that has $3$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{rank}(Q)=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\text{rank}(Q)$ is the number of pivot columns in $Q.$ \n\nSince $Q$ has $7$ columns and $3$ of them are non-pivots, then the number of pivot columns in $Q$ is \n\n$$\n7-3=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(Q)=4.$",
